  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 926 AM MST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nTHE REST OF TODAY:\n\nLight snow will continue to make its way out of the forecast area by \nthis afternoon as the trough axis swings through. Local cameras in \nthe San Juans appear to show a few inches of snow fell overnight, \nwith snow still falling in some locations. Generally, as the \ncloud cover begins to burn off this morning, most locations will\nsee sunny skies and decreased precipitation chances. Otherwise,\ntemperatures have notably dropped behind the frontal boundary \nwhich passed through yesterday. This means that overnight lows \nfor the next several nights are tracking to drop below freezing \nfor a large swath of the area. Any valley locations which have \nyet to hit freezing will likely be hitting it sometime this \nweekend.\n\nSUNDAY + LIGHT SHOWERS EARLY NEXT WEEK:\n\nA low-amplitude ridge builds in behind the exiting trough Saturday \nevening into Sunday morning. This means that Sunday's weather will \nbe relatively similar to Saturday. One point of note would be there \nis a possibility for clearing skies overnight into Sunday morning \nwhich could support localized fog in some valleys. The current \nforecast isn't overly bullish about this factor though, so there \nremains uncertainty. By Sunday evening, upper-level flow turns back \nto southwesterly ahead of an approaching trough. Moisture and \nforcing appear unimpressive with this system, so current \nexpectations are for only light showers Sunday evening through \nTuesday morning. Snow accumulations are on track to sit below \nadvisory level. \n\nThere continues to be a vague signal of another system passing \nthrough late next week, but models are not in good agreement. Some \nsolutions depict wet weather, while others not so much. Therefore, \nthis far out, that forecast should be taken with a grain of salt. \nThis potential storm could impact Thanksgiving travel, so stay tuned \nfor additional updates to the forecast as those dates approach, \nespecially if you plan on traveling for the holiday.",
